<title>NETHERLANDS: FORECAST - Dutch unemployment seen little changed.</title>
<headline>FORECAST - Dutch unemployment seen little changed.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-04-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dutch economists expect unemployment figures for January-March due on Thursday to be little changed compared with December-February.</p>
<p>They forecast that the non-seasonally adjusted unemployment figure for January-March will rise fractionally, while they expect a lower figure for the seasonally adjusted unemployment.</p>
<p>Economists' forecasts are summarised below:</p>
<p>GMT---Date--Period---Indicator---------Consensus--Range----Pvs</p>
<p> 0730  17/4  Jan-Mar  Unemployment NSA  430,000    414-440  429</p>
<p> 0730  17/4  Jan-Mar  Unemployment SA   413,000    396-420  417</p>
<p>Forecasts contributed by: ABN AMRO, Generale Bank, ING, MeesPierson, J.P. Morgan, NIBStrating, Rabobank.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
